From fb0087ce3eab96c20bf222242a543260694be74c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Macktherealonereally <macdev@mackthessd.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:07:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: Close the icon-label gap on large tiles without
 icon background

Large (2x1) tiles center their 28dp icon in a 56dp box so the icons line
up across tiles. Dual target tiles (Bluetooth, Internet, DND...) fill
that box with the icon background, but single action tiles (Auto-rotate,
Flashlight...) draw nothing there, so the empty end of the box pushes
the label far away from the bare glyph.

For tiles without an icon background, leave the 14dp end inset of the
box, (ToggleTargetSize - LargeTileIconSize) / 2, out of its measured
width. The icon keeps its exact position and size and is not clipped;
the label starts as far from the icon as it does from the background on
dual target tiles and gains that width. Placement is start-relative, so
RTL mirrors it. Edit mode scales the inset with the resize progress, so
icon-only tiles are unchanged and resizing has no jump.

Reported-by: SkellyTechs (XDA)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
